WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.639
So here we are in front of the palace, just about to go in.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:07.009
I've got my periodic table tie, so we're
ready to go.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.289
So we're inside the palace, still got the tie,

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:19.829
we're about to go inside.

00:00:19.829 --> 00:00:24.769
No filming inside by us, but I'll tell you what happens afterwards.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.980
Professor Sir Martin Poliakoff

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.520
for services to the chemical sciences.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:00.950
So it was really good, I spoke to Prince Charles,

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:04.140
he asked me about how the green chemistry was going.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.060
I told him that we were making anti-malerial

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.200
drugs, and that we're now doing green chemistry.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.420
We hope to demonstrate using light to induce chemical reactions.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.180
He seemed very interested.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.100
Said he'd like to visit.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.750
When I first got my doctorates and was
called Doctor Poliakoff

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.680
the only reason that I found the
doctorate useful

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.540
was to complain in shops.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.620
If you telephoned and said look you, this is not right.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:53.840
If you said it was Doctor Poliakoff it produced an effect.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.900
Now I have no idea
whether 'Sir' will produce an effect, similar effect,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.410
or whether people will just laugh.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.890
Here we are, outside the palace taking photographs.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.160
And here is the knighthood medal.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.760
I'm quite excited.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.620
And it doesn't look as if it's pure gold,

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.080
but it clearly has some gold in it.

